","E16"]}],"evidenceRequests":["Q3","Q2","Q6"],"summary":"The OTP decline is real: AVL is validated by manual ride checks (E12) and its definition is unchanged (E2). The absenteeism explanation is not supported. The 40% rise is almost entirely a new partial-day recording category (E14), full-day absences rose only 1.1%, and the independent dispatch log shows no change in unoperated trips, late pull-outs or extraboard use (E15). The attendance program would punish recording artifacts, so it is harmful. Early leaves are higher on recovery-cut routes, but seniority and route length confound that (E16). Whether shortened recovery time, construction or ridership drives the decline is unestablished. Route-level AVL OTP before and after April is the key next evidence. Restating the absence data (A4) is the best next action."}}